{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou","id":1159793,"title":"How Widespread is hatred of dogs amongst garou?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-17T05:36:26-08:00","id":1159793,"title":"How Widespread is hatred of dogs amongst garou?","content":"the first edition red talons book has a L:OT of animousity towards dogs in it.<br /> <br /> always assumed that distaste was present, perhaps in less fanatic form, amongst most Garou.<br /> <br /> But in W20 rage Across the world, it shows dog as a totem, and in &quot;Kinfolk: a breed apart&quot; it has a fetish bound with a dog spirit.<br /> <br /> How widespread do you think hatred for the existence of dogs is amongst the Garou? <br /> <br /> Im thinking more pity and disgust, to actually hating dogs as beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T06:58:04-08:00","id":1159819,"title":"","content":"Considering I have seen garou PCs with pet dogs, I don't think dogs are considered to be that bad by most urban homids. After all, a dog spirit is still a respectable spirit of the city and suburbia. Plus, let's be honest, if we look at the genetic make-up of the American wolves... they are wolfdogs more than European ones are (Black coats).<br /> <br /> However, among non-homids and some tribes, dogs might as well be insults. For non-homids, let's face it, it is creepy as it is keeping a mentally disabled eternally immature and physically deformed wolf as an owned being. Dog as a spirit might be ok, but real dogs are creepy. Ironically, I actually imagine Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords being the most insulted by dogs... even though their pure breed does require some dog-like traits to manifest. Red Talons I think see dogs are utter body horror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:03:37-08:00","id":1159854,"title":"","content":"Red Talons still hate how many animals passively accept man's yoke over them, but it's a thing that can influence Lupus-born Garou, tops (obviously, it wouldn't make sense for Homid garou to hate dogs). So yes, dogs are surely the ones despised the most because of how close the species are, but Red Talons also despise cows and horses.<br /> <br /> It's also true the opposite, though: because dogs (and all the other animals) can feel the wolf in the Garou they're going to become restless, bark and maybe even attack if they can sniff a werewolf moving closer enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:07:35-08:00","id":1159855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159854#post1159854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Talons still hate how many animals passively accept man's yoke over them, but it's a thing that can influence Lupus-born Garou, tops (obviously, it wouldn't make sense for Homid garou to hate dogs). So yes, dogs are surely the ones despised the most because of how close the species are, but Red Talons also despise cows and horses.<br /> <br /> It's also true the opposite, though: because dogs (and all the other animals) can feel the wolf in the Garou they're going to become restless, bark and maybe even attack if they can sniff a werewolf moving closer enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the more a homid gets in-tune with their wolf self, the worse they see dogs. Because, again, it is -sorta- wolf. But not quite. They even speak sorta the same signal language as wolves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:43:20-08:00","id":1159872,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UncannyValley\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph.../UncannyValley</a> anyone? <br /> <br /> But that would be more &quot;Makes me kind of uncomfortable&quot;, not &quot;We HATES WE HATES IT WE HATES IT FOREVER!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:57:21-08:00","id":1159878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159872#post1159872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UncannyValley\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph.../UncannyValley</a> anyone?<br /> <br /> But that would be more &quot;Makes me kind of uncomfortable&quot;, not &quot;We HATES WE HATES IT WE HATES IT FOREVER!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that, yeah. More for metis and lupus, given they grew with more reliance to those signals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:02:47-08:00","id":1159880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159819#post1159819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering I have seen garou PCs with pet dogs, I don't think dogs are considered to be that bad by most urban homids. After all, a dog spirit is still a respectable spirit of the city and suburbia. Plus, let's be honest, if we look at the genetic make-up of the American wolves... they are wolfdogs more than European ones are (Black coats).<br /> <br /> However, among non-homids and some tribes, dogs might as well be insults. For non-homids, let's face it, it is creepy as it is keeping a mentally disabled eternally immature and physically deformed wolf as an owned being. Dog as a spirit might be ok, but real dogs are creepy. Ironically, I actually imagine Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords being the most insulted by dogs... even though their pure breed does require some dog-like traits to manifest. Red Talons I think see dogs are utter body horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, Red Talons aside because they hate almost anything, it would be the same thing if human would get repulsed by monkeys kept as pets. So no, i dont think there is any animosity towards dogs in general. Aside from the term being use or being taken as an insult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:12:18-08:00","id":1159882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159880#post1159880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, Red Talons aside because they hate almost anything, it would be the same thing if human would get repulsed by monkeys kept as pets. So no, i dont think there is any animosity towards dogs in general. Aside from the term being use or being taken as an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would akin to having chimpanzee as a pet. So, for some it might be ok, for others, it is too close to a wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:14:20-08:00","id":1159884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159882#post1159882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would akin to having chimpanzee as a pet. So, for some it might be ok, for others, it is too close to a wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to meet a human who thinks chimpanzee as a pet as &quot;keeping a mentally disabled eternally immature and physically deformed human as an owned being&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:45:11-08:00","id":1159892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159884#post1159884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have yet to meet a human who thinks chimpanzee as a pet as &quot;keeping a mentally disabled eternally immature and physically deformed human as an owned being&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Read up on keeping chimpanzees as pets,then, it is often..not as simple as it seems. There is a reason why the lady, whose chimpanzee tore her friend's face off, saw it as her son. As in, they are similar enough that people in a non-zoo enviroment end up treating them as eternal children. Only these kids have sexual urges and if you treat them human enough, yeahh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T11:04:51-08:00","id":1159924,"title":"","content":"Shudders<br /> <br /> allready decided if I could afford an exotic and expensive pet, I'd want a cobra to watch its sinuous graceful movements to feed it live rodents and watch things transpire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:05:46-08:00","id":1159985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159892#post1159892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read up on keeping chimpanzees as pets,then, it is often..not as simple as it seems. There is a reason why the lady, whose chimpanzee tore her friend's face off, saw it as her son. As in, they are similar enough that people in a non-zoo enviroment end up treating them as eternal children. Only these kids have sexual urges and if you treat them human enough, yeahh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but that pears and oranges. Thats the practical complications of keeping them as pets and a very mentally disturbed person. And bad tendency of treating animals as humans and the consequences off all of which dont apply to &quot;dogs and the garou nation&quot; . We, as a society, dont see Chimpanzees as &quot;disabled eternally immature and physically deformed humans&quot; we see them as animals. <br /> <br /> Same i would think of the Garou nation (Blood talons notwithstanding), dog is animal. Useful as pet and guardians and that about it. Even lupus have a hard time relating to actual wolves (as they have an awareness of the self that normal wolves lack) and dogs are even more different.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:16:09-08:00","id":1159989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159985#post1159985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but that pears and oranges. Thats the practical complications of keeping them as pets and a very mentally disturbed person. And bad tendency of treating animals as humans and the consequences off all of which dont apply to &quot;dogs and the garou nation&quot; . We, as a society, dont see Chimpanzees as &quot;disabled eternally immature and physically deformed humans&quot; we see them as animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And anyone who actually is in close proximity to them knows that they're canny, tool-using animals that will cooperate to stage an escape even over an electrified fence. If you underestimate them, they will break out, and in short order. Conversely, if you teach them to dress themselves and take high tea, they will also do this quite admirably (and if they're making a cacophony and throwing things around, it's because humans deliberately set out to lead them to perform these tasks incorrectly for the purposes of spectacle provided to extremely insecure human observers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same i would think of the Garou nation (Blood talons notwithstanding), dog is animal. Useful as pet and guardians and that about it. Even lupus have a hard time relating to actual wolves (as they have an awareness of the self that normal wolves lack) and dogs are even more different.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I think you might want to dial back assumptions of what does and doesn't have an awareness of self, especially if you're playing Werewolf. Human self-awareness is extremely unlikely to have developed from nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:29:44-08:00","id":1159997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159989#post1159989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might want to dial back assumptions of what does and doesn't have an awareness of self, especially if you're playing Werewolf. Human self-awareness is extremely unlikely to have developed from nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That not assumption, that fact. The books mention how Lupus werewolf have a problem fitting in with wolves after the change. Same as Homid breeds when they change with fitting in human society but in another way. Simply put they are now wolves with human level intelligence that the normal wolves lack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-17-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:36:01-08:00","id":1159998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159985#post1159985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but that pears and oranges. Thats the practical complications of keeping them as pets and a very mentally disturbed person. And bad tendency of treating animals as humans and the consequences off all of which dont apply to &quot;dogs and the garou nation&quot; . <b>We, as a society, dont see Chimpanzees as &quot;disabled eternally immature and physically deformed humans&quot; we see them as animals.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded part is my point, garou are also animals. They, no matter how distant their wolf heritage, all understand and can communicate with normal wolves. Imagine being able to do that, and then own a dog. Which is uncanny valley to wolves. Garou are not regular humans, they cannot just turn off their understanding of wolf signals.<br /> <br /> Hence why it would be like owning a chimpanzee, you are with something that is like you but not quite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:43:56-08:00","id":1160001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159998#post1159998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bolded part is my point, garou are also animals. They, no matter how distant their wolf heritage, all understand and can communicate with normal wolves. Imagine being able to do that, and then own a dog. Which is uncanny valley to wolves. Garou are not regular humans, they cannot just turn off their understanding of wolf signals.<br /> <br /> Hence why it would be like owning a chimpanzee, you are with something that is like you but not quite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet Garou arent wolves either, they are in the end their own specie. They arent animals nor humans. They can communicate with wolves but wolves cannot match their intellect. All you are saying of dogs also applies to Wolves. Wolves cannot grasp complex abstract concepts the way humans (and garou) can.<br /> <br /> So much they cannot turn off their understanding of Garou signal, they also cannot turn off their human complex minds and awareness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:48:16-08:00","id":1160003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160001#post1160001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet Garou arent wolves either, they are in the end their own specie. They arent animals nor humans. They can communicate with wolves but wolves cannot match their intellect. All you are saying of dogs also applies to Wolves. Wolves cannot grasp complex abstract concepts the way humans (and garou) can.<br /> <br /> So much they cannot turn off their understanding of Garou signal, they also cannot turn off their human complex minds and awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that complex mind that still understands the wolves and dogs, doesn't feel wrong about -owning- something that you can speak to and acts like an eternally childlike wolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:53:36-08:00","id":1160006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160003#post1160003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that complex mind that still understands the wolves and dogs, doesn't feel wrong about -owning- something that you can speak to and acts like an eternally childlike wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again not in my opinion, just because you can understand it doesnt mean its on the same level as you. A dog is an animal with animal like levels of mental understanding.<br /> <br /> It just means all Garou are the dog whisperers and training dogs is easier. You can bond with a dog, as all humans do but seeing it as &quot;eternally childlike wolves&quot; would take a very mentally troubled garou. Or a Red talon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T14:04:26-08:00","id":1160008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160006#post1160006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again not in my opinion, just because you can understand it doesnt mean its on the same level as you. A dog is an animal with animal like levels of mental understanding.<br /> <br /> It just means all Garou are the dog whisperers and training dogs is easier. You can bond with a dog, as all humans do but seeing it as &quot;eternally childlike wolves&quot; would take a very mentally troubled garou. Or a Red talon.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is what dogs -are- to regular wolves. That's the thing, they aren't -just- animals, unless the garou is willing to say to a lupus packmate that their mother was 'just an animal'. Even if the lupus is smarter than their kin family, they still are their family they grew up with.<br /> <br /> That's what makes the whole thing so interesting to me. Because there is this divide between how a human or a Glass Walker might see dogs. Versus more in-tune with their wolf garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T14:20:14-08:00","id":1160011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160008#post1160008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that is what dogs -are- to regular wolves. That's the thing, they aren't -just- animals, unless the garou is willing to say to a lupus packmate that their mother was 'just an animal'. Even if the lupus is smarter than their kin family, they still are their family they grew up with.<br /> <br /> That's what makes the whole thing so interesting to me. Because there is this divide between how a human or a Glass Walker might see dogs. Versus more in-tune with their wolf garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a tough question because kinfolks both wolf and human are second class citizens and there are a very big part of the nation that regard them as just breeding stock. So would a garou tell his packmate lupus that his mom is just a animal? Not he wont unless he is looking for a fight. Would he think it is? Maybe, maybe not. Hell, the Lupus himself would definetely feel alientated from wolves to a degree between his awareness both mentally and spiritual and his now expanded lifespan.<br /> <br /> So no, i dont think there is a big issue with dogs in the nation. And i havent found anything in the tribebook to support there is beyond the Red talons who also hates cows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:11:54-08:00","id":1160053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160011#post1160011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats a tough question because kinfolks both wolf and human are second class citizens and there are a very big part of the nation that regard them as just breeding stock. So would a garou tell his packmate lupus that his mom is just a animal? Not he wont unless he is looking for a fight. Would he think it is? Maybe, maybe not. Hell, the Lupus himself would definetely feel alientated from wolves to a degree between his awareness both mentally and spiritual and his now expanded lifespan.<br /> <br /> So no, i dont think there is a big issue with dogs in the nation. And i havent found anything in the tribebook to support there is beyond the Red talons who also hates cows.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't many garou NPCs with dogs, though. Bone Gnawers revised outright says that Gnawers HATE being compared to dogs and do not breed with them. Though it is pointed out that there are wolfdogs among the garou.<br /> <br /> But that is honestly aside from my point. Garou Nation possibly wouldn't support having dogs as pets, not only given what they imply, but also as dogs stand for capturing and molding nature to ones use in horrible ways. Not to mention, owning dogs is saying to the lupus population that as far as the owner considers things, wolves can be made into mutants and they consider them free to enslave. That is something I doubt most garou want to do.<br /> <br /> This is on top of the fact that dogs still remain wolf enough to be bred with and to sorta communicate with wolves. They can't just animals to the garou, not when they are far too close to wolves still. Not when there are garou who literally have dog-blood in their veins.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:46:47-08:00","id":1160063,"title":"","content":"Its still gotta be weird though for a Lupus garou looking at say.....an english bulldog....or a shihtzu....or even a mastiff......its something whose ancestors were once like you in form but humans &quot;built&quot; it to never fully mature, to have numerous physical and mental defects that effect its health, longevity and daily life just because the humans found them useful or pleasing to look at, to act as a tool an extension of the human will. Its got to make them a little nervous even if it is more on the uncanny valley side than the kill on sight side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T20:01:51-08:00","id":1160097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160053#post1160053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren't many garou NPCs with dogs, though. Bone Gnawers revised outright says that Gnawers HATE being compared to dogs and do not breed with them. Though it is pointed out that there are wolfdogs among the garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm so? Normal animals are kinda useless with the power level Garou dish and take. Writing a PC with a animal companion is an extra set of stats that dont contribute anything to the game and just generates issues gameplay wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160053#post1160053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is honestly aside from my point. Garou Nation possibly wouldn't support having dogs as pets, not only given what they imply, but also as dogs stand for capturing and molding nature to ones use in horrible ways. Not to mention, owning dogs is saying to the lupus population that as far as the owner considers things, wolves can be made into mutants and they consider them free to enslave. That is something I doubt most garou want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that as other have pointed out. Dog is a valid totem. Also Lupus are a minority in the nation, Lupus themselves are far removed from dogs. They have bigger fish to fry and nothing in the litany makes &quot;having a pet&quot; as bad. Even the GW book mention treats lupus gauru/kin and dogs as 2 distinct species. I doubt the Garou nation would take the time to tell the garous they should kill/get rid of the family dog.<br /> <br /> Also consider that Garou used to do a similar &quot;be made into mutants and they consider them free to enslave&quot; to humans with impergrium (which the blood talons are all in favor of returning). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160053#post1160053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't just animals to the garou, not when they are far too close to wolves still. Not when there are garou who literally have dog-blood in their veins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they can, most garous are homid breeds. They have human minds and human upbringing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160063#post1160063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its still gotta be weird though for a Lupus garou looking at say.....an english bulldog....or a shihtzu....or even a mastiff......its something whose ancestors were once like you in form but humans &quot;built&quot; it to never fully mature, to have numerous physical and mental defects that effect its health, longevity and daily life just because the humans found them useful or pleasing to look at, to act as a tool an extension of the human will. Its got to make them a little nervous even if it is more on the uncanny valley side than the kill on sight side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldnt be just like looking at a Silver Fang lupus/Homid? *ba dum dish*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T20:50:02-08:00","id":1160107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1159997#post1159997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That not assumption, that fact. The books mention how Lupus werewolf have a problem fitting in with wolves after the change. Same as Homid breeds when they change with fitting in human society but in another way. Simply put they are now wolves with human level intelligence that the normal wolves lack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that difficulties fitting in had way more to do with Rage and The Curse than anything else, since those are by far the most apparent signs that everyone picks up on - &quot;This one is dangerous! This one feels wrong!&quot; cuts across both groups of kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:07:06-08:00","id":1160112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160107#post1160107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume that difficulties fitting in had way more to do with Rage and The Curse than anything else, since those are by far the most apparent signs that everyone picks up on - &quot;This one is dangerous! This one feels wrong!&quot; cuts across both groups of kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish i could remember which book it was. But it wasnt just about the rage and the curse (as the latter is irrelevant to wolf kin) but the level of awareness of the self that lupus breed gain couple with their longevity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:17:28-08:00","id":1160115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160112#post1160112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish i could remember which book it was. But it wasnt just about the rage and the curse (as the latter is irrelevant to wolf kin) but the level of awareness of the self that lupus breed gain couple with their longevity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that Werewolf has been very conducive to changing things based on developing understanding of phenomena, mind. It might have said that at some point, but we have those huge appendices on actual animal facts in the backs of breed books for a reason. Werewolf has typically been quite amenable to changing its tune based on changing real world knowledge of animal life and behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:19:25-08:00","id":1160116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160115#post1160115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind that Werewolf has been very conducive to changing things based on developing understanding of phenomena, mind. It might have said that at some point, but we have those huge appendices on actual animal facts in the backs of breed books for a reason. Werewolf has typically been quite amenable to changing its tune based on changing real world knowledge of animal life and behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was one of the last books as i dont read anything before revised era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:30:21-08:00","id":1160337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1159793-how-widespread-is-hatred-of-dogs-amongst-garou?p=1160116#post1160116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was one of the last books as i dont read anything before revised era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the most modern of W:tA books are still set to get older the moment that the text is set and fall out of date in some respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T18:19:43-08:00","id":1160716,"title":"","content":"I can think of at least<i> one </i>reason that Garou (excepting Red Talons, obviously) might not be so stuck up about dogs: Camouflage. The Children of Gaia have that Gift Domestic Seeming, that allows them to pass themselves off as dogs -- specifically <i>Lupus</i> Children of Gaia, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:05:30-08:00","id":1161963,"title":"","content":"I think its a bone gnawer gift &quot;Guise of the hound&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:13:17-08:00","id":1163815,"title":"","content":"I expect lupus would tend to see dogs as an odd, maybe unattractive sort of wolf, and be more bothered by a pug or a basset hound than by a husky or a German shepherd. Imagine what humans would look like a hundred generations into a selective breeding program thst was designed to enhance certain traits or exploit mutations. Maybe Frankenstein's Igor or Quasimodo is starting towards the pug of the human species? Maybe you breed humans for diminutive stature until they weigh less than a house cat - if that is even possible - and you have your human yorkie. Think about how distasteful this sounds, and that's maybe what lupus think of such dog breeds: not really monsters, but not easy to get used to. But then think about how the Chinese government selectively breeds people to produce Olympic athletes. While you might have ethical problems with the human breeding program, it wouldn't bother you to run into one of these athletes on the street. I really do think it is an uncanny valley reaction based on the physical form, and msybe distaste for the manipulative breeding, but it's not really about mental disability -- a dog might not be as good a problem solver as a wolf, but he might have greater social intelligence when interacting with other species. Might be kind of how the modern domesticated human has a smaller brain than prehistoric Cro-Magnon humans, but we have larger frontal lobes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}